 "dayNotes": {
  "2026-10-31": "Halloween Saturday. Meiji Shrine, Harajuku and Shibuya Sky come first.",
  "2026-11-01": "Akihabara and Ginza day.",
  "2026-11-06": "Travel day Kyoto → Nara → Osaka. Both knife shops are close to the hotel but close around 18:00–18:30, so head there soon after check-in. If missed, move to Sat.",
  "2026-11-07": "Main shopping day. Start at Samurai Jeans (opens 11:00, Nakatsu) and work south along the Midosuji line. Dinner is at 19:00 in Hozenji Yokocho, a hard stop. S.A.MUSIC hours are unverified.",
  "2026-11-08": "Derby day. No shopping commitments.",
  "2026-11-09": "Afternoon shopping around Tenjin and Daimyo. Opening hours and closed days are unverified; small shops may have a weekly closing day, check before going. Finish towards Nakasu for the regroup.",
  "2026-11-10": "Sumo comes first if we get tickets. Otherwise free exploring.",
  "2026-11-11": "Travel day. Nothing mandatory. Ochanomizu only if there is energy after the train.",
  "2026-11-12": "Senso-ji early and Kappabashi in the morning, then Shinjuku from about 14:00 with time for proper browsing. Metal and rock shop hours are unverified.",
  "2026-11-13": "Akihabara all day, then the game at 19:00. No vinyl or big purchases before the game: Tokyo Dome allows no large bags and has no cloakroom. Drop anything at the hotel first.",
  "2026-11-14": "Last day, flexible. Choose Shibuya OR Jimbocho if time allows. Luggage, dinner and Haneda (~21:30) come first."
 }
